; The inside case's geometry with `outside`: the line x = 3/8 runs parallel
; to the crest, so the whole spine lies beyond it and the two bodies are
; joined only through the tip. Wrapping the halves around the outside would
; run the reflected crest through both bodies, which the kernel rejects.

paper square

fold --d = map .b onto .a
.m = free on --ab from .a at 3/8
.n = free on --cd from .d at 3/8
.t = free on --d from .[--d --ab] at 1/2
reverse --r = through .m .n moving .t outside

; expect error "reversing the tip would pierce layer"
